WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:23.235
<v Tim / GM>Last time on Cloudfall. Guy and Doran finally hit the ground or should I say the water. They survived but whether they're going to be okay is a different question. They ended up meeting Phenom Green, although at first he appeared as a marshal for the city. Turns out he and his friend Roland are very close with Libera Nimbus, the leader of the free city itself.

00:00:23.955 --> 00:00:38.810
The party played nice and ended up back at Clara's sharing information with Phenom and Roland. For their own safety, the party agreed to set sail today on one of the city's skyships. They're going to a nearby skyland where they should be safe from retaliation by the blight. Should be.

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:31.350
<v Maggie / Poppy>Good morning, everyone.

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:35.590
<v Thomas / Guy>Good morning, Poppy. What's poppin'?

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:38.150
<v Maggie / Poppy>What's poppin'? I've been up since 4AM.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:44.015
<v Tim / GM>It is a bright sunny morning. Phenom seems eager to start shopping for the day.

00:01:44.655 --> 00:01:52.575
<v Maggie / Poppy>I certainly like shopping. Hey, before we go, have some cookies to dole out if, who's afraid of falling?

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:58.460
<v Hannah / Eryn>Aaron is like, you know, in a blanket wrapped around their head.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.140
<v Tara / Journey>I'm barely awake.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.460
<v Maggie / Poppy>Not Aaron then. Okay.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:05.180
<v Thomas / Guy>I recently had an incident involving falling.

00:02:06.085 --> 00:02:07.205
<v John / Doran>Yeah. Same over here.

00:02:07.205 --> 00:02:08.325
<v Thomas / Guy>Dora and you were there.

00:02:08.325 --> 00:02:11.125
<v John / Doran>Right. Yeah. That was not not my favorite part of yesterday.

00:02:11.685 --> 00:02:16.325
<v Maggie / Poppy>Do you guys want to play rock, paper, scissors or Guy, here's a proper Rock.

00:02:17.045 --> 00:02:18.005
<v Thomas / Guy>Thank you, Bobby.

00:02:18.005 --> 00:02:19.605
<v Maggie / Poppy>Do not eat this one right away.

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:36.765
<v Tim / GM>Yes. Pulling it out of his mouth. Phenom sees you all kind of getting your stuff together and getting ready for the day. And he says, we're going to have to make a quick pit stop, if that's okay. There's somebody I want you to meet.

00:02:37.485 --> 00:02:41.485
It it it's Liberia. She wanted to meet you after what happened last night.

00:02:41.885 --> 00:02:46.925
<v Maggie / Poppy>Oh. Wow. Like the the leader of the free city Liberia.

00:02:47.085 --> 00:02:47.885
<v Tim / GM>One and the same.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.080
<v Maggie / Poppy>I don't have anything better than oh gosh, I'm covered in flour.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.160
<v Tim / GM>She's not much of a morning person. She'll be more relaxed the earlier we get there.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.360
<v Thomas / Guy>What is proper protocol for meeting this leader?

00:03:01.775 --> 00:03:02.735
<v Tim / GM>What do you mean?

00:03:02.895 --> 00:03:05.615
<v Thomas / Guy>Do we bow or curtsy?

00:03:05.695 --> 00:03:08.415
<v Tim / GM>She might get a kick out of that. Yeah, do that.

00:03:08.815 --> 00:03:10.815
<v Thomas / Guy>Perfect. Bow then curtsy, yes.

00:03:10.815 --> 00:03:24.280
<v Tim / GM>She's actually fairly relaxed as leaders go. It's not what you'd expect if you've ever been a visitor to a king. It's nothing like that. She's down to earth for as much as she loves the clouds.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:29.000
<v Hannah / Eryn>Do we have to go? I'd rather just lay low.

00:03:32.775 --> 00:03:48.480
<v Tim / GM>Have to is a strong word around these parts, but yeah. Okay. I appreciate it. I understand it might not be comfortable, but again, you're not under arrest, any of you. We'd release you back into the city.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:50.240
We just don't want to clean up the bodies.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:55.440
<v Maggie / Poppy>What exactly does Liberia know about us?

00:03:56.685 --> 00:04:13.630
<v Tim / GM>She knows about last night. We had a little conference after we dropped you off yesterday. She knows what you told us. Basically, that there were some shenanigans with the Bismite and that shadow creature that came from the fake friend.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:16.750
<v Tara / Journey>I call them buds, but you can call them whatever you want.

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:22.510
<v Tim / GM>So she knows a little bit. She knows about Diver and she knows about Eren. Knows that you worked What with the

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.150
<v Hannah / Eryn>does she know about me?

00:04:26.315 --> 00:04:32.795
<v Tim / GM>She has current information. That means she knows that you worked for the blight and that you no longer do. That's the important part.

00:04:34.875 --> 00:04:36.155
<v Hannah / Eryn>Aaron looks unhappy.

00:04:37.675 --> 00:04:43.910
<v Tim / GM>Phenom kind of leans into you Aaron and he says, if it comes down to it, we can do an official pardon. Is that what you're looking for?

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:55.525
<v Hannah / Eryn>I've done a lot of things, you know, to survive in this city. So meeting the person in charge probably is a little

00:04:56.485 --> 00:05:25.325
<v Tim / GM>Roland is in the hallway and he kinda steps in and he says, Aaron, I've been meaning to talk to you a little bit. I mentioned yesterday I've been watching The Blight for a good while, and part of that means I was watching you too. And I know about you, and I know what you can do, and I think it's incredible, and we don't wanna use you for anything. We we want you to be who you are and we just don't want the blight to have you.

00:05:26.765 --> 00:05:29.485
<v Hannah / Eryn>Aaron looks down at their feet for a minute while they think about this.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:34.740
<v Tim / GM>I know you're not the same person you were last night. That's not a surprise to me.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:06:02.520
<v Hannah / Eryn>What I can do, it has only gotten me into bad places. Aaron looks up as they say this to the rest of the group and says, I'm sorry. You guys have been pretty, pretty nice so far. It's it's just been a lot of there's been a lot of Erin kind of trails off and just looks really sad.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:08.840
<v Maggie / Poppy>I think what you can do is really cool. I was, could you turn into me if you want?

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:14.475
<v Hannah / Eryn>Yeah, I could. If you really wanted me to. Wow.

00:06:14.635 --> 00:06:17.035
<v Maggie / Poppy>That's like way, way cool.

00:06:17.035 --> 00:06:22.075
<v Hannah / Eryn>I just have to be really careful. The more people that find out about me, the more danger we

00:06:22.075 --> 00:06:25.115
<v Maggie / Poppy>Count on me. I keep secrets all the time. Right guy?

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:30.580
<v Thomas / Guy>That's right. If it is any consolation, Aaron, I do not wish to hunt you.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.340
<v Hannah / Eryn>Thanks, Guy.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:43.335
<v Tara / Journey>You're also not tied to us. If we all get on this airship and you decide that you're better off going your own way, there's nothing stopping you. But none of us is safe here.

00:06:44.055 --> 00:07:00.070
<v Hannah / Eryn>Aaron just nods. Like last night, we said the blight's coming for us. They know me. Most of them know what I can do, which makes it a little trickier to hide. I think for now, my plan is to go with you.

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:02.950
<v Tim / GM>You hear Phenom and Roland both go.

00:07:05.745 --> 00:07:12.945
<v Hannah / Eryn>Just keeping things on the down low. And I guess we'll go meet the leader of the city. Yeah.

00:07:14.465 --> 00:07:21.000
<v Thomas / Guy>They don't exactly go hand in hand, do they? I dropped my pencil.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:29.720
<v John / Doran>You're saying there's no catch here. I'm sure she wants something from us.

00:07:30.995 --> 00:07:41.635
<v Tim / GM>They look at each other for a second. Phenom says, well, yeah, she wanted to ask you her own questions, but mostly she just wanted to meet you, to get to know you in case she met you again.

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:47.010
<v Hannah / Eryn>Everyone always wants something. Keep that in mind.

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:53.570
<v Thomas / Guy>Phenom, must we wear one of your false images when we meet Libera?

00:07:53.650 --> 00:08:00.495
<v Tim / GM>Not for this. In fact, you should probably come as you are. Well, not completely as you are looking at Doran in his pajamas.

00:08:00.495 --> 00:08:03.455
<v John / Doran>Just need one minute. We can head out.

00:08:04.255 --> 00:08:05.695
<v Maggie / Poppy>Nice bunny slippers.

00:08:06.175 --> 00:08:07.935
<v John / Doran>They take up a lot of pack space, it's worth

00:08:07.935 --> 00:08:10.255
<v Maggie / Poppy>it. They're very comfortable.

00:08:10.815 --> 00:08:15.570
<v Tim / GM>Roland's like, Poppy, it smells so good in here. Are we gonna get these cookies, do we have to wait until

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:25.090
<v Maggie / Poppy>they Don't touch it. Sorry. They're just I put a lot of effort in. These are for my friends. You get me to my shop safely and in one piece, and I will whip some up.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:25.890
<v Tim / GM>We can do that.

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:28.395
<v Maggie / Poppy>Okay. Pleasure doing business with you.

00:08:28.395 --> 00:08:32.795
<v Hannah / Eryn>She made those in the coffee maker this morning, so I don't know how sanitary they are.

00:08:32.795 --> 00:08:33.995
<v Maggie / Poppy>I washed it.

00:08:34.715 --> 00:08:36.635
<v Tim / GM>That is impressive.

00:08:36.875 --> 00:08:41.195
<v Maggie / Poppy>Also, I'm pulling out one of the other cookies and handing it to Doran.

00:08:41.275 --> 00:08:41.595
<v John / Doran>Thank you.

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:43.570
<v Maggie / Poppy>Don't eat this yet either.

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:45.250
<v John / Doran>I really hope I don't eat it today.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:48.290
<v Maggie / Poppy>I give him a toffee temptation. Okay.

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:50.770
<v Tim / GM>Roland is watching with puppy dog eyes.

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:53.570
<v Maggie / Poppy>Sorry. Gotta be part of the gang.

00:08:55.185 --> 00:09:04.705
<v Tim / GM>In a moment, you are all ascending yet another flight of stairs going further up the winged spire to Libera's office. What are you all wearing?

00:09:05.105 --> 00:09:26.065
<v Hannah / Eryn>Aaron only has one set of clothing. Just really simple black kind of tight trousers, black boots that are flat soled, grippy on the bottom, good for climbing. And then kind of a long sleeve black tunic with a cowl, but everything is very worn out. Nothing nothing fancy, nothing to draw attention.

00:09:27.905 --> 00:09:35.745
<v Tara / Journey>Journey is wearing mostly homespun clothes that she clearly made herself

00:09:35.985 --> 00:09:36.305
<v Tim / GM>Mhmm.

00:09:36.465 --> 00:09:48.680
<v Tara / Journey>Some time ago. It's just basically like the rectangles of homemade fabric that are tied to her. She's not super covered, but it's enough to be more like armor. She doesn't really get cold.

00:09:49.785 --> 00:09:51.385
<v Tim / GM>And Guy clinking up the stairs.

00:09:51.385 --> 00:10:06.920
<v Thomas / Guy>Guy is wearing his usual chainmail armor with the green cloak. And what do you think happens to armor when you crash through a building and land in a pool of water? Probably polished but scuffed. Okay. Yeah.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:10.280
Looking polished but scuffed from the events the day before.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:23.175
<v John / Doran>Doran is wearing just his gambeson, which is very form fitted and wearing some nice pants. That's it. The pants

00:10:23.175 --> 00:10:26.935
<v Maggie / Poppy>are nice. I was worried there weren't pants. I was like waiting.

00:10:27.015 --> 00:10:28.375
<v Tim / GM>So it is armor or?

00:10:28.375 --> 00:10:30.215
<v John / Doran>It's the Under Armour for It's

00:10:30.215 --> 00:10:33.410
<v Tim / GM>very medieval. It's under armor. Right.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:34.130
<v Maggie / Poppy>Yeah. Yeah.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:35.730
<v John / Doran>Exactly.

00:10:36.850 --> 00:10:37.570
<v Tim / GM>Poppy?

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:55.025
<v Maggie / Poppy>Poppy has like a poofy little yellow dress that she normally wears, but she has taken off her apron and hat and like tucked them away because they are well used and covered in flower and little blue glasses.

00:10:55.905 --> 00:11:01.425
<v Tim / GM>Suffice to say a motley crew, ranging from actual solid armor to literal rags.

00:11:01.425 --> 00:11:01.665
<v Thomas / Guy>Hey.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:03.640
<v Tara / Journey>Hey. Hey.

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:18.595
<v Tim / GM>As you take these hundreds of stairs going up to Liberia's office, you understand how she's earned her reputation for taking bridges and lifts and flying inventions to go up and down the tower on the daily.

00:11:18.835 --> 00:11:21.235
<v Hannah / Eryn>Was this where we stayed? The same building? Same building.

00:11:21.235 --> 00:11:23.075
<v Tim / GM>Yep. The Winged Spire.

00:11:23.075 --> 00:11:24.195
<v Hannah / Eryn>Okay. Thank you.

00:11:24.275 --> 00:11:25.795
<v Maggie / Poppy>That's an awful lot of stairs.

00:11:26.630 --> 00:11:50.225
<v Tim / GM>On your way up, can see out the window, there's these enormous canvas wings on the side of this tower. Literally the wings on the Spire. These things catch air as it blows and indicate the direction and speed of wind to kind of give a little heads up to all the airship people in the city of like how rough it is out there today. So pretty much a giant weather vane on a colossal scale. Cool.

00:11:50.625 --> 00:12:14.205
That is the last thing you see before you get to Libera's office. Large violet double doors that open up. And when they do, you see another huge floor to ceiling bay window that looks out over the clouds from an even higher vantage. Turning around, you can see the windows actually continue around the entire room. And when you spin around, you can see the entire city of Farewell laid out behind you.

00:12:14.765 --> 00:12:29.980
Libera herself is facing you. She is kind of half sitting on the front of her desk, but she's speaking with an old man with white hair. She's wearing common looking workers' clothes. It's like a canvas jacket. And then she's got red and violet official garb underneath that.

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:44.255
And she's got long black hair tied into a braid. She says, I know it doesn't feel good, but it was the right decision. Of course, they're upset right now. They're disappointed. The violet dragon flight means a lot to them.

00:12:44.975 --> 00:13:05.835
You hear, you are very kind with your words. The old man goes, and kind of looks behind him. Your your words about the violet dragonflight. If I meet one of them, a violet dragon, I will tell them that you said this, that people are upset and disappointed. What I meant is that this will pass.

00:13:05.915 --> 00:13:19.870
Don't worry. Liberia kind of looks up and sees all of you enter the room at the same time. She goes, I apologize. My meetings are overlapping with each other. My friends, please, may I introduce you to farewell, the man himself?

00:13:20.510 --> 00:13:22.590
Every bit the founder of the city as I am.

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:27.070
<v Thomas / Guy>Your highness and guy bows and curtsies.

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:28.910
<v John / Doran>Dorne Dorne does as well.

00:13:29.745 --> 00:13:33.825
<v Hannah / Eryn>Bows and curtsies? What does that look like exactly? A bow.

00:13:33.825 --> 00:13:34.945
<v Tim / GM>At the same time? Yeah.

00:13:34.945 --> 00:13:38.145
<v Hannah / Eryn>A bend and then the arms go out with no skirt. Okay.

00:13:38.145 --> 00:13:50.210
<v Tim / GM>The white haired man bows and curtsies to you as well with a big smile. He says, yes, greetings to you all. It's true. I found this city at the same time as Libera.

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:53.410
<v Maggie / Poppy>I found this city. Though

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:56.210
<v Tim / GM>it was not really a city back then.

00:13:57.335 --> 00:13:58.375
<v Thomas / Guy>What was it?

00:13:59.255 --> 00:14:14.760
<v Tim / GM>It was merely a plot of land that Liberia found, and then I found it as well. And we are both here, and we own it together. What is that? Ah. Ah.

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:22.680
Very good. Yes. Time is of the essence. Well, time to go. I have to go.

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:27.105
Farewell. Farewell. Farewell. Farewell.

00:14:27.105 --> 00:14:28.625
<v John / Doran>Nice to meet you, farewell.

00:14:28.625 --> 00:14:33.745
<v Tim / GM>As he's walking away, every time you say farewell, turns back to you and just kind of nods to you.

00:14:34.705 --> 00:14:36.145
<v Maggie / Poppy>Was a little bit weird.

00:14:37.825 --> 00:14:46.590
<v Tim / GM>Libera says, I'm sorry about that. Uh-huh. So you're the group that faced down Diver. Is that right?

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:49.150
<v Maggie / Poppy>Define face down.

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:50.750
<v Tara / Journey>He got away.

00:14:51.230 --> 00:14:52.350
<v John / Doran>He did escape.

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:54.670
<v Maggie / Poppy>I didn't personally face him down.

00:14:55.375 --> 00:14:56.575
<v John / Doran>Oh, there's a bit

00:14:56.575 --> 00:14:58.895
<v Thomas / Guy>of facing and definitely some down.

00:14:59.055 --> 00:15:07.455
<v Tim / GM>Yes. And he's gone now? Dead? What is the situation? Definitely not dead.

00:15:07.455 --> 00:15:15.750
<v John / Doran>He flew away in his own airship. I don't even think he necessarily needed to retreat. It was not going as planned.

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:17.510
<v Thomas / Guy>I could have had him.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:18.710
<v Maggie / Poppy>Definitely.

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:32.715
<v Tim / GM>She seems to be kind of sizing you up, kind of assessing your injuries to see if you really could have taken him. Well, let's start in a proper position. I am Libera Cambria Nimbus, and I'm not sure I've met any of you before.

00:15:33.835 --> 00:15:46.150
<v Maggie / Poppy>Well, it's really nice to meet you. And I curtsy. I'm Poppy Kenmore and I own cookies. I mean, cookie shot the rolling pin. That's me.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:49.670
<v Tim / GM>I have heard whisperings of the rolling pin.

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:51.350
<v Maggie / Poppy>Good ones, I hope.

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:55.655
<v Tim / GM>Always good. Yes. Absolutely. Yes. Proud to have you and farewell.

00:15:55.655 --> 00:16:02.215
<v Maggie / Poppy>Thank you so much. You're very welcome. I mean, I'm welcome. I mean, you're very nervous.

00:16:03.255 --> 00:16:04.855
<v John / Doran>It's quite an accusation, Poppy.

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:09.750
<v Tim / GM>No, she's right. Who are you?

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:14.790
<v John / Doran>I'm Doran, just a humble blight hunter. I've been here in farewell.

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:21.955
<v Tim / GM>A blight hunter. Brilliant. She kind of like looks you up and down. She says, Dawn's Edge.

00:16:22.435 --> 00:16:23.715
<v John / Doran>What gave me away?

00:16:25.075 --> 00:16:27.955
<v Tim / GM>Hair, clothes, the way you're standing.

00:16:28.515 --> 00:16:30.195
<v John / Doran>You kind of have a little bit of that too.

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:35.450
<v Tim / GM>You'd be right. That's good though. You'll be in good company.

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:39.050
<v John / Doran>Wait, is that where we're headed with the airships?

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:47.625
<v Tim / GM>Not exactly. You're going with Dawn's Edge, not to Dawn's Edge. Let's finish our introductions. Who do we have here?

00:16:48.665 --> 00:16:49.865
<v Thomas / Guy>I am Guy.

00:16:52.985 --> 00:16:53.945
<v Tim / GM>And who is this?

00:16:55.460 --> 00:17:02.580
<v Tara / Journey>You can call me Journey. My name wouldn't we don't really do names where I'm from, but Journey will work.

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:05.700
<v Tim / GM>Ah, Fjerbulk. Am I correct?

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:06.980
<v Tara / Journey>Indeed, you are.

00:17:07.875 --> 00:17:14.195
<v Tim / GM>Interesting. I have met very few Fjerbug in my days. If I make a mistake, please let me know.

00:17:14.515 --> 00:17:16.755
